# Harness rules

The template owns this file (agent-harness {{ harness_ref }}) and `copier update` replaces it: never edit it here,
put project facts in CLAUDE.md. Everything else is derived: `uv run dev --help` lists commands,
`docs/generated/agent-surface.md` lists agents, skills, hooks, plugins and MCP servers, `docs/research/INDEX.md` lists
what is already researched.

## Every session
- A SessionStart hook injects `uv run dev orient` (handoff, board, worktrees, memory, quota). Run it again after long breaks.
- The board is GitHub issues: `uv run dev board next`, `board brief <n>`, `board claim <n> --agent <name>`.
  Work without an issue does not exist. Each issue has a measurable DONE WHEN. A small fix found on the way
  belongs to the current issue: the fix-now rule (multi-agent.md §3).
- The main session is the **lead** for its machine. It plans, dispatches and integrates (the `harness-ops:lead`
  skill), and it never builds while workers run. Workers are `harness-ops:` subagents, one issue each, in their own
  worktree.
- Multi-agent and multi-machine protocol: [multi-agent.md](../docs/specs/multi-agent.md).

## Rules
- Python is managed with **uv only** (`uv add`, `uv run`), never pip. A hook enforces this.
- Branch `<issue>-<slug>` in a worktree. Never commit to `main` directly. Only `uv run dev integrate <pr>` merges.
- Run `uv run dev test --affected` while iterating. Run `uv run dev check` once at the end, on a committed tip.
  Never weaken a check, test or budget to pass. Ask the owner instead.
- **Research before implementing.** Any design or algorithm choice needs a cited note in `docs/research/`.
  Check INDEX.md first and extend an existing note rather than writing a parallel one. Use the research skill.
- **Reuse before build.** Name libraries you know and verify them: `uv run dev reuse check <name>...`. Search
  (`uv run dev reuse "<need>"`) only when you know no good candidate or want more. Prefer free and open source.
  Record the choice, its license and the alternatives in the note.
- Label claims **VERIFIED** (measured here, script named), **SOURCED** (cited and fetched), **BELIEVED** (judgment)
  or **ASSUMED**. Never cite a source you did not fetch. `uv run dev cite-check` must pass for changed notes.
- Re-check a root cause with data before writing it down. First explanations are often wrong.
- Navigate by symbol: `uv run dev code outline|show|refs|find`. Do not read whole files. A hook answers whole-file
  reads of long files with an outline.
- Batch independent reads and searches as parallel tool calls in one response.
- Never edit generated files (`docs/generated/`, `docs/research/INDEX.md`, `uv.lock`); run `uv run dev docs`.
  Never read `.env`.
- Facts live in one place. Link to them; do not copy counts, field lists or commands into prose. The gate fails on
  dangling paths and unknown `uv run dev` commands.
- Hand-backs are at most 25 lines. Details go in the PR body or an issue comment.
- Unclear requirement: add it to `docs/questions/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md` with your default, then proceed on that default.

## Changing the agent surface
CLAUDE.md, this file, `.claude/`, `.devkit/`, `[tool.devkit]` and CI are the harness every agent is judged by. Follow
the `harness-ops:harness` skill: keep text short, keep word budgets (`.devkit/ratchets.toml`) falling, and measure
with `uv run dev agent-stats`. Generic changes go to agent-harness itself, then `copier update` here. A PR that
touches harness files needs the lead to read its diff.
